:: Robin Console Visit
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
<<npc Robin>><<person1>>
You head down the hall and knock on Robin's door. <<He>> answers after a moment, brightening the instant <<he>> sees you.
<br><br>
"I got a new game on my console," you say, "and a spare controller. Want to come play in my room?"
<br><br>
"Really? Yes!" <<He>> ducks back inside and returns with <<his>> own controller tucked under one arm.
<<He>> follows you back to your room and flops onto your bed, getting comfortable.
<br><br>
You switch on your console and hand <<him>> a controller.
<br><br>
<<set _rng to random(1, 3)>>
<<if _rng is 1>>
	You load up a cooperative game and work through it together, covering for each other's mistakes. The hours slip by easily.
	<<stress -3>><<lstress>>
<<elseif _rng is 2>>
	You pick something competitive. Robin is annoyingly good, and <<he>> beats you again and again, giggling each time.
	<<npcincr Robin dom 1>><<gdom>>
<<else>>
	You pick something competitive and, to <<his>> visible dismay, trounce <<him>> round after round. <<He>> pouts, but can't stay grumpy for long.
	<<npcincr Robin dom -1>><<ldom>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if Tamagotchi.isAlive()>>
	<<link [[Show Robin your virtual pet|Robin Console Visit Pet]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Play late into the evening (2:00)|Robin Console Visit Late]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Wind down (0:45)|Robin Console Visit End]]>><</link>>

:: Robin Console Visit Pet
<<effects>><<set $outside to 0>><<set _t to Tamagotchi.status()>>
You show Robin the little virtual pet living in your console. "This is <span class="blue">_t.name</span>," you say.
<br><br>
Robin leans in, utterly charmed. "It's adorable! You have to look after it properly, you know." <<He>> shows you a few tricks for keeping it happy.<<npcincr Robin love 1>><<glove>>
<br><br>
<span class="green">_t.name seems to perk up from all the attention.</span>
<br><br>
<<link [[Back to the game|Robin Console Visit Late]]>><</link>>

:: Robin Console Visit Late
<<effects>><<set $outside to 0>>
<<pass 120>>
You sprawl out together and lose track of time, swapping the controller back and forth long into the evening. It's the most relaxed you've felt in ages; the worries of the day melt away as you laugh at <<his>> terrible jokes.<<stress -20>><<trauma -10>><<lstress>><<ltrauma>>
<br><br>
Eventually Robin yawns and stretches. "I should head back before Bailey notices," <<he>> says, gathering up <<his>> controller. "That was really fun. Let's do it again." <<He>> gives you a warm, sleepy smile.
<<npcincr Robin love 2>><<glove>><br><br>
<<link [[Next|Bedroom]]>><<unset $consoleAction, $trainType>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Robin Console Visit End
<<effects>><<set $outside to 0>>
<<pass 45>>
After a while you both set the controllers down and just talk for a bit.<<stress -6>><<lstress>>
<br><br>
"Thanks for inviting me," <<he>> says, gathering up <<his>> controller. "That was really fun. Let's do it again." <<He>> gives you a warm smile before heading back to <<his>> own room.
<<npcincr Robin love 1>><<glove>><br><br>
<<link [[Next|Bedroom]]>><<unset $consoleAction, $trainType>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Alex Console Visit
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "alex_cottage">><<effects>>
<<npc Alex>><<person1>>
You hold up your console and ask Alex if <<he>> wants to play the virtual pet game with you.
<br><br>
<<if C.npc.Alex.dom gte 15>>
	Alex stares at the little screen, then at you. "You're joking." <<His>> jaw tightens. "I've got animals out there that'll die if they're not fed, fences that need mending, and you want me to <i>babysit a cartoon</i> with you?"
	<br><br>
	<<He>> turns away, plainly irritated that you'd waste both your time on a toy when there's real work on the farm. "Grow up." <<npcincr Alex love -2>><<npcincr Alex dom 1>><<lllove>><<gdom>>
<<else>>
	Alex squints at the little screen, baffled. "What... is that? A pretend animal?" <<He>> looks genuinely puzzled. "We've a whole farm of <i>real</i> animals that need looking after, and you're fussing over a fake one?"
	<br><br>
	<<He>> shakes <<his>> head and wanders off, no closer to understanding the appeal. <<npcincr Alex love -1>><<llove>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Farm Bedroom]]>><<unset $consoleAction, $trainType>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Robin Console Gift
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
<<npc Robin>><<person1>>
"Here," you say, holding out your own console. "I want you to have this one."
<br><br>
Robin's eyes go wide. "What? No, I couldn't! It's <i>yours</i>."
<br><br>
You press it into <<his>> hands and insist. <<He>> stares down at it, then clutches it to <<his>> chest and throws <<his>> arms around you, sniffling.
<br><br>
"Thank you. Thank you so much. I'll look after it, I promise." <<He>> wipes <<his>> eyes, already itching to set it up.
<<npcincr Robin love 15>><<npcincr Robin dom -1>><<npcincr Robin trauma -10>><<glove>><<ldom>><<lrtrauma>>
<<set $robinconsole to 1>>
<<if V.furniture.bedroom and V.furniture.bedroom.console>>
	<<run delete V.furniture.bedroom.console>>
<<elseif V.furniture.cottage and V.furniture.cottage.console>>
	<<run delete V.furniture.cottage.console>>
<</if>>
<<if not Furniture.get("console", "bedroom") and not Furniture.get("console", "cottage")>><<run Tamagotchi.bury()>><</if>>
<<unset $consoleAction, $trainType>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin's Room Entrance]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Robin Arcade
<<effects>><<set $outside to 0>><<set _robin to statusCheck("Robin")>>
<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	"Would you like to go to the game centre?" you ask.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"Let's hit the arcade," you say.
<<else>>
	"Want to go to the game centre?" you ask.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if Time.hour lt 12 and (Time.schoolDay or Time.isWeekEnd())>>
	<<effects>>
	<<His>> eyes light up, but then look at the clock on the wall. "I can't," <<he>> says. "I need to get ready soon. I can go in the evening."
	<br><br>
	<<robinoptions>>
<<else>>
	<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "town">><<effects>>
	<<set $daily.robin.arcade to 1>><<money -1000 "robin">><<pass 30>>
	<<His>> face lights up. "The arcade? I love that place!" <<He>> springs to <<his>> feet.
	<br><br>
	<<if $robinromance is 1>>
		You walk hand in hand to Starfish Street. The bleeps and jingles of the amusement arcade spill out onto the pavement before you even reach the door.
	<<else>>
		You walk together to Starfish Street, the bleeps and jingles of the amusement arcade spilling out onto the pavement before you even reach the door.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	Inside, the machines beep and whirr around you. Robin's eyes dart everywhere at once. "What should we play first?"
	<br><br>
	<<link [[A racing cabinet|Robin Arcade Play]]>><<set $phase to 0>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[A co-op shooter|Robin Arcade Play]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[The prize machines|Robin Arcade Play]]>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Robin Arcade Play
<<effects>><<set $outside to 0>><<pass 45>>
<<switch $phase>>
	<<case 0>>
		You squeeze into the twin racing seats and thumb a coin into the slot. Robin takes the bends recklessly, shrieking with laughter every time <<he>> clips a barrier, and somehow still beats you on the final lap.<<stress -12>><<lstress>>
		<<npcincr Robin love 1>><<glove>>
	<<case 1>>
		You stand shoulder to shoulder at a co-op light-gun cabinet, covering each other against waves of pixelated horrors. Robin's a surprisingly good shot, and the two of you clear the final stage to a tinny fanfare.<<stress -12>><<lstress>>
		<<npcincr Robin love 1>><<glove>>
	<<default>>
		You drift over to the prize machines, feeding coins into the claw and the coin-pusher. Robin presses against your shoulder, willing the claw to grip. When a plush finally tumbles down the chute, <<he>> cheers loud enough to turn heads.<<stress -12>><<lstress>>
		<<npcincr Robin love 1>><<glove>>
<</switch>>
<<unset $phase>>
<br><br>
<<set _hasConsole to (Furniture.get('console', 'bedroom') or Furniture.get('console', 'cottage'))>>
<<if _hasConsole and random(1, 100) lte Tamagotchi.boosterChancePct()>>
	<<set _boost to Tamagotchi.rollBooster()>>
	On the way out, Robin lingers at a gachapon machine and feeds in the last of <<his>> coins. The capsule that rattles out makes <<him>> gasp.
	"Look! It's a booster pack for that virtual pet!"
	<br><br>
	<<He>> presses it into your hands, and you crack it open together right there on the pavement.
	<br><br>
	<span class="gold">Robin gave you <<= _boost.label>> <<= _boost.detail>>!</span><<ltrauma>><<trauma -3>>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<if $robinromance is 1>>
	You leave the arcade hand in hand, ears still ringing pleasantly, and head back to the orphanage.
<<else>>
	You leave the arcade together, ears still ringing pleasantly, and head back to the orphanage.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Options]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Console Rescue
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
<<npc Robin>><<person1>>
<<set _resc to Tamagotchi.claimRobinRescue()>>
<<set _t to Tamagotchi.status()>>
Robin's eyes light up the instant <<he>> sees you, and <<he>> scrambles to <<his>> feet and rushes over,
throwing <<his>> arms around you.
<br><br>
"You're back! I knew it. I just knew you'd come home." <<He>> holds you tight.
"I kept telling myself you'd turn up sooner or later... so I looked after <span class="blue">_t.name</span> while you were gone.
Fed it, kept it clean, all of it."
<br><br>
<<if _resc.keyGained>>
	<br><span class="gold">Robin presses something into your hand too that <<= _t.name>> turned up while you were away;
	a dungeon key! You now hold <<= _resc.keys>>.</span>
<</if>>
<br><br>
You thank <<him>>, and <<he>> beams, still not quite ready to let go.
<<npcincr Robin love 1>><<glove>><<trauma -6>><<stress -10>><<ltrauma>><<llstress>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Bedroom]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
